{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011sVw4KDrcL7hGtVhXWxKLw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# T06: FX conversion and currency-specific precision\n2\t\n3\t## Business relevance\n4\tFloat arithmetic, unsupported currencies, and one-size-fits-all cent rounding can misstate international payments.\n5\t\n6\t## Requirements\n7\tImplement `convert(amount: str, source: str, target: str, rate: str) -> dict`. All monetary inputs and rates are decimal STRINGS (never floats). Currencies and minor-unit scales: USD=2, EUR=2, JPY=0, KWD=3. `amount` must represent a positive finite amount exactly expressible in the SOURCE minor units, allowing additional trailing zeros; `rate` must be a positive finite decimal. Reject unknown currencies, numeric rather than string inputs, negative/zero amounts or rates, and fractional source minor units with ValueError. Compute target value using exact decimal arithmetic `Decimal(amount) * Decimal(rate)`; round once to the TARGET minor-unit scale using ROUND_HALF_EVEN. Return exactly {\"target_minor\": int, \"target_amount\": fixed-width decimal str, \"rate\": unchanged rate str}. Example: USD 1.01 at rate 0.5 to USD gives 0.50, 50 minor units (banker's rounding). No network access or FX lookup; caller-supplied rate is authoritative.\n8\t\n9\t## Deliverable\n10\tEdit only `service.py` in the provided workspace. Keep the public function signatures described above. Use Python 3.11+ standard library only. Outcomes are graded on behavior; any valid implementation is accepted.\n11\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"22f7b7b9-f358-44c8-a9c4-21b92c10fa0c","uuid":"5ee2dfff-d17c-4ec2-89d3-3865912a3b74","timestamp":"2026-11-08T17:48:30.802Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/fs/8s8c9g190t770b0xnpg810dh0000gn/T/txn-T06-1sbqrw6g/workspace/INSTRUCTION.md","content":"# T06: FX conversion and currency-specific precision\n\n## Business relevance\nFloat arithmetic, unsupported currencies, and one-size-fits-all cent rounding can misstate international payments.\n\n## Requirements\nImplement `convert(amount: str, source: str, target: str, rate: str) -> dict`. All monetary inputs and rates are decimal STRINGS (never floats). Currencies and minor-unit scales: USD=2, EUR=2, JPY=0, KWD=3. `amount` must represent a positive finite amount exactly expressible in the SOURCE minor units, allowing additional trailing zeros; `rate` must be a positive finite decimal. Reject unknown currencies, numeric rather than string inputs, negative/zero amounts or rates, and fractional source minor units with ValueError. Compute target value using exact decimal arithmetic `Decimal(amount) * Decimal(rate)`; round once to the TARGET minor-unit scale using ROUND_HALF_EVEN. Return exactly {\"target_minor\": int, \"target_amount\": fixed-width decimal str, \"rate\": unchanged rate str}. Example: USD 1.01 at rate 0.5 to USD gives 0.50, 50 minor units (banker's rounding). No network access or FX lookup; caller-supplied rate is authoritative.\n\n## Deliverable\nEdit only `service.py` in the provided workspace. Keep the public function signatures described above. Use Python 3.11+ standard library only. Outcomes are graded on behavior; any valid implementation is accepted.\n","numLines":11,"startLine":1,"totalLines":11}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011sVw4KDrcL7hGtVhXWxKLw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
